section: ghci
synopsis: Make external interpreter communication use an explicit Async RPC
issues: #27960
mrs: !16802

description: {
    iserv already implements RPC today, although in a fairly ad-hoc and
    convoluted manner. The template haskell consumer already requires
    bidirectional communication and async requests, and got implemented in a
    way that precludes other consumers with async needs.
    This change streamlines all this by using an explicit Async RPC protocol.

    It additionally clears the path to fix #18852 since the main thread is no
    longer blocked per request, enables evaluating splices concurrently in the
    external interpreter, and unblocks multi-threaded interactive debugging.
}

